/-!
# Local permutation geometry for the A₇ exclusion

The action is constructed from the actual C-component quotient, relative
normality in H, and the two-group supplement supplied by 13.8.21. Its
restriction to K is computed on representatives. The marked actors and
their conjugates are transported through H → H/O₂(H), with an exact
comparison of local two-cores. A natural transvection forces the faithful
seven-point action to be surjective and is incompatible with placement
of a conjugated actor in the four-plus-three two-core.

The source local reduction now excludes case (1) of 13.8.8 and proves the
case-(2) partition dichotomy for the actual L₁*T*. Solvable stabilizers lift
through O₂(H), 13.8.13 places their lifts in M, and L₁ = θ(H∩M) upgrades
containment to equality. The natural module in the first case is selected
from all three 13.8.5 alternatives and transported through the same change
of coordinates. The factor of nine comes from the actual E₉ quotient.
The quotient action, component marking, Sylow orbits and critical-actor
conjugates are retained. The KL₁T reduction preserves relative normality
and the original component quotient.

All earlier source clauses used by the reduction are explicit mathematical
inputs. The two remaining partition contradictions belong to the parent
assembly; this module does not assert the final A₇ exclusion.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
13.8.24, printed pp.958–959 (combined manuscript, 1 March 2004).
-/
